.TH AWCCCTL 1 "October 2026" "AWCC Linux 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
awccctl \- Universal Linux Hardware Performance, Fan Control & Telemetry Utility
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B awccctl
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fISUBCOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B awccctl
is the command-line interface for the AWCC Linux performance and cooling ecosystem.
It provides hardware detection, platform profile management, fan boost offset
control, Game Shift (G-Mode) toggling, low-level CPUID hardware interrogation,
cycle-accurate RDTSC bus latency diagnostics, and real-time streaming telemetry.
.PP
Hardware support spans Alienware/Dell G-Series, ASUS ROG/TUF, Lenovo ThinkPad/Legion,
HP OMEN, Acer Predator/Nitro, MSI Gaming, Framework, System76, and standard Linux desktop motherboards.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B detect [\-\-json]
Detect hardware interface, active provider, and vendor DMI information.
.TP
.B status [\-\-json]
Display the complete telemetry matrix including CPU and GPU compute utilization, clocks,
temperatures, package and board power, RAM, battery, and fan speeds.
.TP
.B battery, quiet, balanced, performance, ultra [\-w|\-\-watch] [\-m|\-\-monitor]
Direct single-command profile and fan boost actuation:
\fIbattery\fR (low-power + 20% boost),
\fIquiet\fR (acoustic silence + 40% boost),
\fIbalanced\fR (daily productivity + 60% boost),
\fIperformance\fR (high workload + 80% boost),
\fIultra\fR (maximum cooling & Game Shift + 100% boost / 255 Max RPM).
When passed \fB\-\-monitor\fR or \fB\-\-watch\fR, transitions directly into real-time telemetry streaming.
.TP
.B profile [\fIPROFILE\fR] [\-w|\-\-watch] [\-m|\-\-monitor]
Get or set the active ACPI platform performance profile (e.g. \fIquiet\fR, \fIbalanced\fR, \fIperformance\fR).
When actuated with \fB\-\-monitor\fR or \fB\-\-watch\fR, streams continuous telemetry.
.TP
.B fan \fIboost\fR <\fIINDEX\fR> <\fIBOOST\fR>
Set the fan boost offset (0\(en255) for the designated fan index (1=CPU, 2=GPU).
.TP
.B fan max
Engage maximum cooling turbines across all discovered fans (255/255 boost or disengaged mode).
.TP
.B fan release
Release fan overrides back to automatic firmware/BIOS thermal control curves.
.TP
.B gmode [status|on|off|toggle]
Control or query Alienware Game Shift (G-Mode) instantaneous high-performance state.
.TP
.B track, monitor [\-\-interval <\fISEC\fR>] [\-\-json] [\-\-once]
Continuously stream live hardware telemetry in real time. Terminate cleanly with \fBCtrl+C\fR.
.TP
.B capabilities [\-\-json]
Inspect auto-detected hardware classification, tier, provider adapter, and available controls.
.TP
.B doctor
Run comprehensive system diagnostic checks, verify sysfs file security permissions (0644/0755),
probe CPUID assembly leaves for DTS and HWP Speed Shift, and measure sub-microsecond ACPI read latency via RDTSC.
.TP
.B verify [\-\-step\-duration <\fISEC\fR>]
Execute a 5-step fan ladder calibration sequence to verify tachometer RPM response.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print help information and exit.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH PRIVILEGE BOUNDARY
Hardware actuation requires root privileges mediated through \fBsudo\fR, PolicyKit
(\fBpkexec\fR / \fIio.github.monkey0_9.awcc.pkexec\fR), or the \fBawccd\fR background daemon.
Sysfs nodes remain strictly non-world-writable (\fB0644\fR).
.SH SEE ALSO
